Link qdoc as a position independent executable.

POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE is switched off for qdoc because a static
libclangTooling.a may not be PIE. With the clang libraries shared that does not
apply, and the -no-pie link then fails under ThinLTO, whose code generation
assumes a static relocation model for objects compiled with
-fno-direct-access-external-data:

  ld.lld: error: cannot preempt symbol: qt_version_tag

--- a/src/qdoc/qdoc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/qdoc/qdoc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -353,7 +353,6 @@
 
 # If libclangTooling.a is not built with -fPIE enabled we cannot link it to qdoc.
 # TODO: Re-enable PIE once clang is built with PIE in provisioning.
-set_target_properties(${target_name} PROPERTIES POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE FALSE)
 
 qt_internal_extend_target(${target_name} CONDITION (WIN32 AND ICC) OR MSVC
     LINK_OPTIONS
